{"dog":{"age_group":"adult","application_url":"https://www.nycacc.org/adopt/adoption-process/","availability_detail":"available","breed_display":"Medium mixed breed","breed_primary":"Medium Mixed Breed Cross","description_text":"My Boroughbreaker writes: Adelaide is an absolute sweetie and cuddlebug. On our Central Park walk, she was eager to greet any human who showed her any attention. We pretty quickly learned Adelaide's trademark move is fully leaning her head and body into anyone who stopped to pet her and gazing adoringly into their eyes. She melted several hearts that way. Adelaide walked relatively well on a leash (she did pull here and there, but not much more than other dogs I've dog-sat for friends). In the home, Adelaide was quiet and calm the entire time. With zero fuss, she let my boyfriend and I give her a warm soapy washcloth rub-down with gentle rinse, then spent the rest of the afternoon cuddling with us on the couch. Adelaide was also quick to trust us with belly rubs and hugs (and in fact, she was the one who instigated them!). Whenever one of us left the room, she would matter-of-factly hop off the couch to look for where we went (more curious than anxious), but otherwise enjoyed snuggling and napping on the couch.","detail_url":"https://nycaccpets.shelterbuddy.com/animal/animalDetails.asp?s=adoption&searchTypeId=4&animalType=3%2C16&pagesize=75&task=view&tpage=15&searchType=4&animalid=210408","id":"841a9a06ee002c0d11b754807ec6ffb0","image_urls":["https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/664211752bd840c98b251c83c56ebdc1-1794177455-1794177477-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/6e8733ddae054864a78576404813d55c-1794177455-1794177455-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/ca6f842499ec468a98215098fec37a64-1794177454-1794177454-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/3c33657a69474ecbb04477c76cac2cd4-1794177454-1794177454-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/imag